{
  "dom_id": "step-t8168",
  "name": "The Division Sign in Algebra",
  "problem": "The **quotient** of two numbers means that we need to divide the first number by the second number.\n\nFor example, \"the quotient of $x$ and two\" means the same thing as \"$x$ divided by two\" and can be written as either expression below:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{x}{2} ,\\qquad x \\div 2 \\, .\n$$\n\nIn algebra, we prefer to represent division using the fraction bar instead of the ($\\div$) symbol.",
  "worked_solution": "",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
